src/context/view.ts\" \"src/durable/context/edits.ts\" \"src/durable/context/view.ts\" \"src/renderers/context-entries.ts\" \"test/durable/context-planning.test.ts\" \"test/globals/session-edits.test.ts\"","status":"done","output":"","code":0},{"id":9,"traceSequence":12,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"add\" \"--\" \"src/context/imitated-calls.ts\" \"test/globals/imitated-calls.test.ts\"","status":"done","output":"","code":0},{"id":10,"traceSequence":13,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"diff\" \"--cached\" \"--name-only\" \"--no-renames\" \"-z\"","status":"done","output":"CHANGELOG.mddocs/reference.mdsrc/context/boundary.tssrc/context/edits.tssrc/context/imitated-calls.tssrc/context/view.tssrc/durable/context/edits.tssrc/durable/context/view.tssrc/renderers/context-entries.tstest/durable/context-planning.test.tstest/globals/imitated-calls.test.tstest/globals/session-edits.test.ts","code":0},{"id":11,"traceSequence":14,"command":"git \"commit\" \"-m\" \"Notice replies that write an elided-call record instead of calling a tool\\n\\nRefs #409\"","status":"done","output":"[fix/409-imitated-elided-calls 0e140fc] Notice replies that write an elided-call record instead of calling a tool\n 12 files changed, 263 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n create mode 100644 src/context/imitated-calls.ts\n create mode 100644 test/globals/imitated-calls.test.ts\n","code":0},{"id":12,"traceSequence":15,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"rev-parse\" \"HEAD\" \"--abbrev-ref\" \"HEAD\"","status":"done","output":"0e140fcfcf00e870b925e191a6c1c3ce70b9cda3\nfix/409-imitated-elided-calls\n","code":0},{"id":13,"traceSequence":16,"command":"git \"--literal-pathspecs\" \"rev-parse\" \"--abbrev-ref\" \"--symbolic-full-name\" \"@{u}\"","status":"done","output":"fatal: no upstream configured for branch 'fix/409-imitated-elided-calls'\n","code":128},{"id":14,"traceSequence":17,"command":"git \"push\" \"-u\" \"origin\" \"fix/409-imitated-elided-calls\"","status":"done","output":"remote: \nremote: Create a pull request for 'fix/409-imitated-elided-calls' on GitHub by visiting:        \nremote:      https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/new/fix/409-imitated-elided-calls        \nremote: \nTo https://github.com/cv/pit\n * [new branch]      fix/409-imitated-elided-calls -> fix/409-imitated-elided-calls\nbranch 'fix/409-imitated-elided-calls' set up to track 'origin/fix/409-imitated-elided-calls'.\n","code":0},{"id":15,"traceSequence":18,"command":"gh \"pr\" \"list\" \"--state\" \"open\" \"--limit\" \"1\" \"--head\" \"fix/409-imitated-elided-calls\" \"--json\" \"number,url\"","status":"done","output":"[]\n","code":0},{"id":16,"traceSequence":19,"command":"gh \"pr\" \"create\" \"--title\" \"Notice replies that write an elided-call record instead of calling a tool (#409)\" \"--body\" \"Refs #409. Not closing yet: this changes what the model and the transcript see, so it needs a live Pi check first.\\n\\n## Reproduction\\n\\nThe issue gives enough to reproduce this without the session file. Its step 4 test is the trigger: a completed assistant message whose last text line is an `[Pit: elided tool call…]` record and that has no `toolCall` block. Before this change, Pit's `turn_end` boundary returned nothing for such a message, so the run settled with no tool result and no notice. The new test `test/globals/imitated-calls.test.ts` builds that exact message on a real Pi `SessionManager`. A mutation probe that disables the notice makes its two positive tests fail (`expected undefined to be true`).\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **Detect it and say so (proposal 1).** `src/context/imitated-calls.ts` flags a completed reply that makes no tool call and whose last line starts with the elided-call prefix. At `turn_end`, Pit appends a `pit.imitated-call` notice saying no tool ran and the action did not happen, and returns `continue: true` so the model gets one more response to make the call.\\n  - **Loop guard:** if the reply right after a notice repeats the mistake, it gets the notice again but no continuation. A later slip, after a normal reply, counts as new.\\n  - **Not flagged:** a reply that also makes a tool call, a record quoted inside prose or a code block, and an aborted reply.\\n  - **What the user sees:** a one-line warning, `▲ No tool ran · the reply ended with an elided-call record, not a call · Pit asked the model to make the call`. The expanded view shows the model-facing text.\\n- **Say in the record that it isn't a call (proposal 3).** Elided-call records now end with `· already ran; writing this text runs nothing`, on both Pi and pi-durable. The prefix is unchanged, so edits already in sessions are still recognized as elided.\\n- CHANGELOG and `docs/reference.md` are updated.\\n\\n## Not in this PR\\n\\n- **Proposal 2** (a stub format the model never writes itself) would undo #292's choice of not leaving a copyable stub call. Better to wait and see whether 1 and 3 are enough.\\n- **Proposal 4** (a session-analysis count) needs a new field in the `sessions.readEvents` jq projection. It's a good follow-up for measuring before and after.\\n- **pi-durable:** these hosts get the new record text but not the turn-end check.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- [x] `delivery.validate({ coverage: true, packageCheck: true })`: check, tests, coverage, and package check all pass\\n- [x] Mutation probe on the new tests\\n- [ ] Live Pi check: `/reload`, have a reply end with a record and no call, and confirm the warning row and that the model continues once\" \"--base\" \"main\" \"--head\" \"fix/409-imitated-elided-calls\"","status":"done","output":"https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/410\n","code":0}],"traces":[{"id":1,"sequence":1,"namespace":"__pit","method":"savedFunctionRun","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":25}],"startedAt":1794998507978,"status":"succeeded","function":{"invocationId":1,"name":"delivery.listChangedFiles","scope":"project","depth":1},"durationMs":0},{"id":2,"sequence":2,"namespace":"shell","method":"execFile","arguments":[{"t